https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

You are free to copy, distribute, transmit and adapt these databases
under the ODbL, including the share-alike duty for any adapted database
and the attribution duty for a produced work.

sea_tss.bin also contains schemes added from printed public regulations
(33 CFR 166 and 167, NGA Pub. 157, COLREG.2/Circ.44) where the
OpenStreetMap extract had no geometry. Those supplements are not
OpenStreetMap. They are named in SOURCE.md and in scripts/supplements.py.

sea_zones.bin also contains IMO and domestic limit polygons closed on
the Natural Earth coast (public domain). The OpenStreetMap part of that
file is the china-yangtze record. See SOURCE.md.

UKHO, Admiralty, and MARNET data are not in these files.
